      "purposeInStoryline": "Lessons 1–3 established the three trigonometric ratios and the complementary-angle relationship. Lessons 4–6 applied those ratios to find unknown sides and angles in worked problems. Lesson 7 is the bridge lesson: learners translate abstract ratio knowledge into a physical measuring instrument and verify it against a real structure, consolidating every prior lesson and positioning them to complete the full phenomenon investigation in Lesson 8.",
